Reduced Server Disk Usage from 83% ➡️ 38% (Real-World DevOps Optimization)

As a DevOps Engineer, I recently tackled a performance issue on one of our production servers where disk usage hit 83% due to heavy Docker usage — containers, images, CI/CD pipelines, and build cache piling up over time.

🔍 Root Cause:
Docker had accumulated dangling images and unused build cache
CI/CD pipelines left behind large build artifacts

🛠️ What I Did:

# Checked disk usage and Docker's footprint
sudo df -h
sudo docker system df

# Cleaned up unused Docker resources
sudo docker image prune -a -f       # Removed unused & dangling images
sudo docker builder prune -a -f     # Cleared build cache

📉 Result:

 ✅ Brought down disk usage from 83% to 38%
 ✅ Optimized Docker environment for faster builds and better resource availability
💡 Docker + CI/CD can fill your disk faster than expected — regular cleanup is essential for stable infrastructure!
